# Restricted Nested-Repair Morphism Contract

This contract prevents a lower object from being called a projection of an
upper repair source merely because their dimensions, spectra, or cohomology
agree. Every promoted bridge must identify the map and certify the rows below.

## Object record

Each object must declare:

| Field | Required content |
|---|---|
| `base` | admissible configuration stratum or finite substitute |
| `typing` | principal symbol, domains, boundary data, sector, branch, descent |
| `inner` | graded algebra/category, module, first-order `Q`, curvature `Phi=Q^2` |
| `pairings` | star/real structure, cyclic trace, Hilbert metric, normalization |
| `shared_line` | line, connection, holonomy/weight action |
| `outer` | scalar `V`, Witten differential, adjoint, positive square |
| `transfer` | filtration and the allowed `m_n` convergence/truncation rule |
| `target` | literal lower operator/object, not only an isomorphic carrier |

## Arrow record

A dimension-reducing arrow records `p,i,h` and must pass:

| Gate | Exact obligation | Failure means |
|---|---|---|
| `R0 typing` | preserve symbol, domain, stratum, descent and branch | only an untyped analogy |
| `R1 contraction` | `pi=1`, `Qh+hQ=1-ip`, side conditions | no controlled reduction |
| `R2 first order` | intertwine `Q` and `Q^*` | spectra/squares may hide phase |
| `R3 curvature` | intertwine `Phi=Q^2` and Jordan/Lie shadows | different defect source |
| `R4 normalization` | preserve unit, cyclic pairing, metric and declared `V` | scalar replay or rank artifact |
| `R5 shared line` | preserve connection, holonomy and weights | merely isomorphic circles |
| `R6 outer repair` | intertwine Witten differential, adjoint and both squares | Hessian/kernel not same-source |
| `R7 transfer` | declare `p,i,h`, filtration, convergence and transferred `m_n` | interactions inserted downstream |
| `R8 target` | equal the accepted typed target operator | benchmark only |

## Strict versus transferred data

The following are strict intertwining claims:

```text
p Q=Q_H p,
p Phi=Phi_H p,
p d_V=d_(V_H) p,
p H_V=H_(V_H) p.
```

Higher products obey a different statement. They are computed from transfer
trees containing `p,i,h`; they need not be strict images of source operations.
For example, a source DGA may have no primitive `m3` while the target has a
nonzero transferred `m3`. Every ledger entry must use the word `transfer` for
that situation.

## Evidence levels

```text
formal definition
  < exact local witness
  < local theorem plus exhaustive certificate
  < overlap/descent theorem
  < selected continuum-to-finite intertwiner
  < accepted physical target and independent prediction.
```

Passing a lower level never changes the truth value of a higher one.

